## [RULE:MULTI-TENANCY] Tenant Isolation Pattern (Multi-Tenancy)
<!-- SECTION:tenant_isolation -->

**Critical rules — flag any violation HIGH severity (cross-tenant data leak):**

### Rule 1 — `_apply_tenant_filter(stmt)` is the only correct guard

It is fail-closed: raises `ValueError` if `tenant_id` is `None`, preventing accidental cross-tenant queries. Every query on a tenant-scoped repository must call it.

### Rule 2 — New tenant-scoped repositories must inherit `TenantAwareRepository`

If a new entity has a `tenant_id` column, its repository must inherit from `TenantAwareRepository` and call `_apply_tenant_filter()` on every query.

